   "from": "Dan Hong",
   "author": "b983b9bbef7f7acb",
   "date": "2014-08-06T19:26:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: Run App button",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">David Hood, a Community TA from Coursera&#39;s Developing Data Products course, helped me figure it out. I had two Shiny R files, ui.R and server.R, in my working directory in addition to all my other regular R script files which confused RStudio into thinking all the files were Shiny files. So, I just moved the two aforementioned files into a subfolder and restarted RStudio and, voila, the default run buttons came back!</div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
